WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:09.840
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:20.370
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.560
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:07.040
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:14.310
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:21.050
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:21.050 --> 00:01:28.480
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:59.760
<b>The Door to a New World</b>

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.080
I’ve never seen
such insubordination!

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:28.700
This is why I was against
disbanding Rubor and Caput!

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.030
We cannot afford to rely
solely on Chor Tempest!

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:36.600
Gather all our troops and Similes!

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.200
The patrol Similes and the
cruise Similes. I want them all!

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.220
Yes, sir!

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:42.970
What a fool.

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.220
Conflict will not
bring about a solution.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.340
Onasia…

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:27.690
I told you not to do that!
Stop playing with the Simoun!

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:30.380
Huh? So how come?

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:31.660
How come?

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:33.980
Well, because…

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:36.860
Let’s see…

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.660
What’s that?

00:03:41.660 --> 00:03:45.280
It’s making a sound,
like it’s humming!

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.370
No way!

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.100
Hey, you’re right!
It’s humming.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.840
It sounds like a whistle!

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.380
You too, Rimone!

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.840
Well? Well?

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:09.570
I can hear a humming sound.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.560
Right? Right?

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:45.740
I see…

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.760
So that day has finally come.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.540
Please give us a little time.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:57.310
Would you mind waiting
until we’ve finished eating?

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:06.160
Have negotiations
broken down then?

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.950
Onasia is the symbol
of Simulacrum Kyuukoku.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:12.620
Undoubtedly it is to our
superiors’ advantage that she…

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.580
…maintain her current silence.

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:18.970
Nevertheless, should Onasia
decide to make a move…

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:22.090
I certainly don’t enjoy conflict.

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:23.260
Even so…

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:26.480
Bringing Onasia here
at a time like this…

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.600
I just don’t understand what the
high priestess could be thinking.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.560
Guragief…

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.890
Suppose I…

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:36.850
Never mind…

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:59.330
Taking off in the Simouns
without authorization…

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.630
…is an unprecedented infraction!

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:03.840
Where is your sense
of responsibility?

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:05.830
Responsibility?

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:09.010
Do we recognize that we’re Simoun
sibyllae and take pride in that?

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:12.100
Yes, I would say that’s true
of each and every one of us!

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.730
Is that all you have to say to us?

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:21.610
If so, please excuse us.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.250
You little brats!

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.000
Paraietta…

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:46.000
Vura…

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.510
And Roatreamon and Alty, too!

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:51.500
Just as we thought, Paraietta…

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:54.510
You couldn’t sleep either, huh?

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:56.230
Neither could we.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.390
Para-sama…

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.720
Hey, is the whole gang here then?

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.690
We shall send Onasia
back on the Messis.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:44.230
Sibylla Neviril, Sibylla Aer…

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.190
May I ask you to join us?

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:54.410
Do you not want to know more
about that different world?

00:07:57.070 --> 00:07:58.630
Me too…

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.080
Will you take me too?

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:01.660
Um…

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:04.670
No, we cannot go in
such great numbers.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.180
Please.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:27.400
Is it good?

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:29.730
Um…

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:32.030
I’m not sure…

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:33.940
…I’d call it good.

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:38.160
It’s a little bitter, I think.

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:41.170
And it’s also a little bit sweet.

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:45.040
But it’s not that
I don’t like it.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.360
I think…

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.210
…I can finish it all.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:51.960
“I don’t know…”

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:53.470
What?

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:56.390
You’ve stopped saying
that all the time, Rimone.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.580
Yes…

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.140
I’m starting to realize…

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:03.250
…that if you really think about it,
there’s nothing you can’t understand.

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.270
That’s why…

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.600
I’m the opposite.

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:11.980
The more I think about
something, the more lost I get.

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:15.280
Dominüra…

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:22.410
All right, let’s finish eating,
and then we’re going.

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.620
Where?

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.290
I don’t know.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:35.180
The high priestess
has ordered us…

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:37.260
…to make this as smooth
a flight as possible.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.300
Right.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.830
I wonder where we’re headed.

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:55.570
What do you want?

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:56.750
Um…

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:00.670
Onasia-sama is at rest now.

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:01.920
Let her in.

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:20.680
Onasia?

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:25.200
Why did she bring up
the “different world”?

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.680
That high priestess…
There’s something about her.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.600
Sure, the military councilor’s
an annoying old man too…

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.150
…but that high priestess…

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.690
…I don’t know…

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:39.450
What?

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.180
Your hands…

00:10:42.180 --> 00:10:43.450
…they’re so small.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.460
Don’t treat me like a kid!

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:52.880
War makes things that
should be obvious…

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:54.670
…so very hard
to see, doesn’t it?

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.470
Onasia…

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.980
There is something
you wish to ask me.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:12.810
You told me that you
could hear Mamina’s voice.

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:15.150
So… what about my comrades?

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:20.780
Have their souls been released?

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:27.740
The one who really
wishes to be released…

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.240
…is you yourself.

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:36.670
By placing yourself at the
brink of your comrades’ deaths…

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:40.760
…you are actually trying to flee
as far as possible from those deaths.

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:55.020
Onasia-sama…

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:56.610
We seem to have arrived.

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:44.750
Why the Ruins?

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:54.410
There it goes again.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:56.830
The door to a new world!

00:12:57.600 --> 00:13:00.350
The melody played
by that music box…

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:05.930
…as well as the unintended destination
of those who lost their lives here.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:06.800
What?

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:08.180
That’s right…

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:11.060
This was once the training
ground for Chor Dextra.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.810
Chor Dextra?

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:15.770
Sibylla Aer…

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:18.770
…that was the chor your own
grandfather served as regina for.

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:21.270
Grandpa… a regina?

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:38.000
Can I ask you something?

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.130
Yes.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:40.670
That day…

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:42.450
What happened that day?

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:44.530
What day?

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:46.010
On the Messis…

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.010
It all came surging back…

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:51.760
What?

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.890
The moment I looked into
the helical motors…

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.680
It was as if I was seeing…

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:57.850
Somebody’s…

00:13:57.850 --> 00:13:59.760
The memory of something…

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:05.150
What you see there is
nothing but a helix.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:08.490
As it turns out, the only thing
we’re capable of understanding is…

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.170
Sibylla Dominüra?

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.920
Dominüra…

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:40.650
And then we became enthralled
with Ri Majons… and the Simouns.

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:44.400
But that was because we had nothing
but the Simouns to cling to…

00:14:45.120 --> 00:14:46.160
That’s right…

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:49.110
If the Simouns had never
existed in the first place…

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:52.060
Or even if they had existed…

00:14:52.060 --> 00:14:54.700
…but no one ever
discovered how to use them…

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:55.910
…then what would have happened?

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:58.680
Huh? Well…

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:00.660
Um…

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:02.150
I think…

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:04.920
I think…

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:19.020
We brought them here!

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.470
We brought them here!

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.040
They’re here!

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:42.250
Long, long ago, there was a
civilization far superior to ours.

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:46.710
And it is said that the Simouns
were in existence at that time.

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:51.190
But after a succession
of wars broke out…

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:53.230
…the country was left in ruins.

00:15:54.110 --> 00:15:56.260
And once all of the lands
were rendered worthless…

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.810
…there was no longer
any reason to wage war.

00:15:59.480 --> 00:16:02.130
The starving multitudes no
longer needed the Simouns…

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:03.950
…and eventually they
forgot how to use them.

00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:06.600
The people…

00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:09.940
…had no choice but to wait for
certain destruction at nature’s hands.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:18.520
It was then that something
broke through the sky…

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:20.830
…and a Simoun arrived
from a different world.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:26.000
On board that Simoun
were two children of God.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.290
These young girls…

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:33.260
These young girls announced
themselves as “Simoun sibyllae.”

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:34.310
And…

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:37.050
They then shared the secret
of the Emerald Ri Majon!

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.100
The Emerald Ri Majon?

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:40.500
That’s right.

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:41.970
To a different world…

00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:46.560
No, that which transports one to a
different time, the ultimate Ri Majon!

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:51.070
It is a divine gift.
A magnificent “if.”

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:55.890
What if during that era…

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:58.830
…they had told the people
that another war was coming?

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:02.400
If the Simouns hadn’t existed…

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:05.330
…then I might never
have existed either.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.700
If, during that era…

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:10.340
…they found a way to convince the
people of the need for Simouns…

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:18.240
But if I’d never existed…

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:21.220
…then this pain never
would’ve existed either.

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:25.060
This era so full of hardship
and strife might be changed.

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:27.690
To transcend time and space…

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:31.020
…and offer this
“if” to some other era.

00:17:31.020 --> 00:17:33.190
That is precisely the purpose…

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:36.570
…of the Simouns and
of the Emerald Ri Majon.

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.570
Transcend time and space?

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:40.970
Unbelievable… How could that…

00:17:40.970 --> 00:17:44.330
Wait a minute! Then what about this
Chor Dextra you say my grandpa led?

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:46.620
Chor Dextra…

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:50.840
…was created for the sole purpose
of completing the Emerald Ri Majon.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:54.840
Someone you know very well was
also a former member of this chor.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:58.130
Sibylla Dominüra…

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:01.850
She is the last surviving
member of Chor Dextra.

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:07.840
Dominüra?

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.060
That’s right.

00:18:10.060 --> 00:18:12.360
I had the misfortune to find out…

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.250
That everything…

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:26.000
That everything that
happened started with me.

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:45.310
Just now…

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:49.810
I thought about what
you just said, Dominüra.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:52.720
You know, if the Simouns
had never existed…

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:55.550
If they hadn’t?

00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:57.150
Yes.

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:00.740
Then I never would’ve met
everyone in Chor Tempest.

00:19:00.740 --> 00:19:02.490
And, Dominüra…

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.570
…I never would’ve met you.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.460
Why are you crying?

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:16.630
I wonder why?

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:17.800
Well…

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:19.090
Um…

00:19:19.090 --> 00:19:20.630
Because you’re sad?

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:22.300
Because you’re lonely?

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:24.020
Because it hurts?

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:25.430
What else…

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:26.650
Let’s see…

00:19:28.470 --> 00:19:30.520
Because you’re happy?

00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:32.760
That’s right.

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:34.490
Because I’m happy.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:39.770
Let’s go.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:43.280
You mean go without
knowing where again?

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:44.530
No.

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:46.130
I do know where.

00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:12.230
<i>Under the blue sky.</i>

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:17.940
<i>Beyond the white clouds.</i>

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:23.460
<i>It’s as blue as a tear.</i>

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:28.820
<i>As white as a lily.</i>

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:34.650
<i>In the pitch-black darkness.</i>

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:40.320
<i>The light of a red flame.</i>

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:49.430
Sibylla Dominüra most likely
completed the Emerald Ri Majon.

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:50.930
Then you mean…

00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:53.040
She is alive in another time.

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:59.270
Sibylla Dominüra and Sibylla
Rimone are both alive.

00:20:59.270 --> 00:21:01.690
I am certain that they are.

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:02.750
Then…

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:05.610
Amuria…

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.700
Then…

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:11.290
…does that mean that Amuria
may also be alive somewhere?

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:19.710
The Emerald Ri Majon was a
divine gift. Our only hope…

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:23.200
Whether it will take us into the
future or back into the past…

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:25.220
That is not for us to know.

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:27.520
However…

00:21:27.520 --> 00:21:31.470
…it is by the will of the gods of
Tempus Spatium that the Simouns exist.

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:33.630
Therefore…

00:21:33.630 --> 00:21:35.980
…the gods cannot be mistaken.

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:41.680
I am positive that they will
open the door to the correct era.

00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:43.530
Sibylla Neviril…

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:44.990
Sibylla Aer…

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:47.310
I would like to…

00:21:47.310 --> 00:21:48.700
…entrust this task to you.

00:21:50.470 --> 00:21:52.490
The Emerald Ri Majon!

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:03.000
Get a move on!

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:07.970
You say it’s a Simoun
from the Arcus Niger?

00:22:08.690 --> 00:22:09.730
Military councilor!

00:22:09.730 --> 00:22:11.970
What’s the meaning of this?

00:22:12.960 --> 00:22:14.360
The Arcus Niger…

00:22:15.490 --> 00:22:16.720
…was shot down.

00:22:17.230 --> 00:22:18.500
Wha?

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:22.480
Seven o’clock! Five ancient
Simouns approaching fast!

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:23.480
What in the world?

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:48.000
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:52.240
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:59.310
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.310 --> 00:23:06.900
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.720 --> 00:23:19.790
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.970
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:28.940
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:32.980
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.980 --> 00:23:38.850
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.850 --> 00:23:44.390
<i>Soar away into the
sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.390 --> 00:23:47.830
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.830 --> 00:23:53.490
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:59.720
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:06.670
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:06.170 --> 00:24:08.500
The Shoukoku-Plumbum highlands allied forces…

00:24:08.500 --> 00:24:10.590
…have begun their
invasion of Kyuukoku…

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:12.800
…and the attacks are
increasing by the day.

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:15.510
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:20.020
<b>Sortie</b>

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:17.810
Sortie.
